#!/usr/bin/env bash

# Memory System Help Documentation

cat << 'EOF'
MEMORY SYSTEM HELP
==================

## OVERVIEW

The 'mem' command is a comprehensive memory management system for organizing
AI conversations, decisions, knowledge, and project documentation.

## USAGE

mem <command> [arguments]

## COMMANDS

📝 CONVERSATION MANAGEMENT
save-conversation "title"
Create a new conversation template with proper frontmatter
Example: mem save-conversation "API Design Discussion"

export-conversation
Show detailed instructions for exporting Cursor conversations
Includes workspace-specific export commands

export-latest
Export the most recent Cursor conversation for current project
Requires cursor-history (chi) to be installed

export-all
Export ALL conversations for the current project
Automatically filters and organizes by project name
Adds proper frontmatter and moves to memories/conversations/

move-exported <file-path>
Move an exported conversation file to the memories directory
Adds proper frontmatter and metadata
Example: mem move-exported /tmp/conversation.md

📋 DECISION MANAGEMENT
create-adr "title"
Create an Architecture Decision Record (ADR) template
Example: mem create-adr "Use React for Frontend"

extract-decisions
Scan conversations for potential decisions
Helps identify when ADRs should be created

🧠 KNOWLEDGE EXTRACTION
extract-knowledge [file]
Extract insights from a conversation file
Identifies decisions, tasks, and knowledge automatically
Example: mem extract-knowledge conversations/meeting-notes.md

📅 DAILY WORKFLOW
process-daily
Analyze today's daily note and suggest next steps
Automatically categorizes content (issues, plans, tasks, knowledge)
Provides actionable recommendations

🔍 SEARCH & ORGANIZATION
search "query"
Search across all memory files for specific terms
Example: mem search "authentication"

list [type]
List all items of a specific type
Types: conversations, decisions, tasks, knowledge, plans
Example: mem list decisions

🔧 SYSTEM INTEGRATION
check-github
Check if GitHub integration is available
Shows status of .github directory and gh CLI

## INSTALLATION REQUIREMENTS

- cursor-history (chi): pnpm install -g @johnlindquist/cursor-history@latest
- GitHub CLI (optional): brew install gh

## DIRECTORY STRUCTURE

memories/
├── conversations/ # AI conversation exports
├── decisions/ # Architecture Decision Records (ADRs)
├── knowledge/ # Extracted insights and facts
├── tasks/ # Action items and todos
├── plans/ # Project strategies and roadmaps
├── journal/ # Daily notes
└── templates/ # Reusable templates

## WORKFLOW EXAMPLES

1. DAILY WORKFLOW:
   mem process-daily

   # Analyzes today's note and suggests actions

2. CONVERSATION EXPORT:
   mem export-all

   # Exports all project conversations with proper metadata

3. DECISION CAPTURE:
   mem create-adr "Database Choice"

   # Creates ADR template for architectural decisions

4. KNOWLEDGE EXTRACTION:
   mem extract-knowledge conversations/meeting-notes.md

   # Processes conversation for insights

5. SEARCH & DISCOVERY:
   mem search "authentication"
   mem list decisions
   # Find relevant information across all memories

## FRONTMATTER FORMAT

All memory files use YAML frontmatter for AI processing:

---

type: conversation|decision|knowledge|task|plan
category: ai-discussion|adr|insight|action|strategy
project: project-name
created: YYYY-MM-DD
status: draft|proposed|accepted|archived
tags: [tag1, tag2, tag3]

---

## TROUBLESHOOTING

- "memories directory not found": Run basic-memory setup first
- "cursor-history not installed": Install with pnpm command above
- "No conversations found": Ensure you're in correct project directory
- "GitHub CLI not available": Install with brew install gh

For more help, see the memory system documentation in memories/knowledge/
EOF
